WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:05.230
No matter how far away we are

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:10.110
We can come together

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:14.160
La la la la

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.610
One Two Three Four Fly

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.610
One Two Three Four Fly

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.860
Fly

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.780
Fly

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.640
Okay, good!

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.410
Good job!

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.680
Good work!

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:33.850
Good job!

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.750
Good work. You were great.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.180
Thank you.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.280
Makoto, is something wrong?

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:40.920
I'm the same as ever.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.390
No problems.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.720
<i>Will all my singing ever reach that person?</i>

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.360
<i>What should I...</i>

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.830
Hey, Makoto,

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.660
we have another job offer.

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:56.770
You'd visit a restaurant and experience cooking first hand.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.040
Not every job has to be about singing, right?

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:01.740
Fine.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.340
But I have one condition.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.440
A condition?

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:12.180
Happy go lucky girls! Precure! Yeah!

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.650
The world is like a merry-go-round

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.520
Love makes it turn, 3, 2, 1

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.560
Every day it sparkles

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.260
Dokidoki Precure

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:30.140
I wear my new clothes and walk a path I've never walked before

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.810
My heart races and I greet the scenery around me

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:41.450
The color of the flower on the corner will be my lucky color for the day

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:46.890
Leave it all to me, because today I'm blessed

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.590
If your friends are in trouble

00:01:52.790 --> 00:02:01.470
isn't it normal to help them?

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.140
Happy lucky Precure

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:05.540
Only Precure makes my heart pound

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.370
Our happy love will change the world

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.180
What's more than just cute

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.050
is our promise between girls

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:21.090
I will fight for you and believe in you

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.990
Gather your unparalleled tenderness, yeah, Precure

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.000
Hold The Phone!

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.000
Hold The Phone!

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.210
Huh?

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.410
What's this?

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.380
A TV shoot?

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.590
Wow!

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.100
That's what I said!

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.510
I hear they were dead set on our shop,

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.750
so they picked it right away!

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.720
As the Pig Tail's second generation chef, {I konw the shop is Pig's Tail, but that doesn't flow right here. Normally, in regular conversation, you'd just drop the first possessive, no?}

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.560
I've gotta keep a steady hand!

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.620
Don't worry!

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.430
Your cooking's the best in Japan!

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.420
Well, not on <i>my</i> watch.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.950
Come on, Dad.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.040
You know an idol's coming,

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.730
so greet her with a smile!

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.020
An idol?

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.100
Who's coming?

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.100
Hm, I think it was...

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:17.650
Hello.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:18.880
Good morning.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:19.780
Makopi!

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.310
This is great!

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.710
I had no clue you were visiting my house!

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:29.010
I only came for business.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.920
Is this your house?

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:31.900
Yeah!

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.960
I'm Aida Mana!

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.960
Just call me Mana!

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.870
I'm Hishikawa Rikka.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.300
All right then,

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.000
we'll start filming tomorrow,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.990
so we're gonna rehearse it today!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.000
R-Right!

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.110
I hope we work well together.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.400
You can do it, Daddy!

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.570
Uh, now then,

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:54.220
today's challenge is our famous omelette rice! {60p? But you're already recording in 1920x1080.}

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.010
First, we have to prep.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.530
Dice the onions and carrots,

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.790
and thinly slice the bacon and mushrooms.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.000
So, can you wash the carrots for me?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:06.760
Sure!

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.120
D-Don't use detergent!

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:13.690
Please?

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:14.740
Huh?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.590
I'm terribly sorry!

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.440
Makoto has never cooked before...

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:23.400
Well, that's just how first timers are.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.480
So, how about cutting the bacon next?

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:27.800
Cutting?

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.350
Let's begin.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:40.350
Makoto, you're not a samurai...

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:40.980
Huh?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.850
I'm terribly sorry!

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.830
Makoto has truly never cooked before!

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.630
Well, that's just how first timers are.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.630
Let's move on!

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.030
Oh yeah!

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:50.870
How about we crack the eggs!

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:52.990
Lower the difficulty!

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.100
Oh, then...

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:57.950
I'll crack them. {Cut away to Mana cringing due to explicit gore}

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:08.230
That couldn't have been on purpose.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.200
No, it was.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.950
Makoto's eyes are dead serious.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.200
Makopi,

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.920
you've gotta handle food with lots of love!

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.770
Huh?

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.790
This is food?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.760
What did you <i>think</i> it was?

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:26.800
What kinda chef doesn't know you can eat an egg?

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.320
Start over!

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.370
Grandpa! {Said by Mana}

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.370
Dad! {Said by Mom. You don't have to add this if it's too difficult.}

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.550
Well, that's enough for today,

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.640
so we'll start filming tomorrow.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.570
What a mess.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.920
Will Makopi even come tomorrow?

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:46.170
Should we start thinking up a backup plan?

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:49.080
Well that was unexpected!

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.060
Didn't think she was <i>that</i> bad at cooking.

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.770
It's not a matter of skill.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:58.440
Dad likes to put his heart into his cooking.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.130
His heart?

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.960
When you face the cutting board, you cook with the person eating it in mind. {starts on "tokoton"}

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.340
That's what cooking is.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.080
I'm sorry about that.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.600
Lately, you've been singing non-stop,

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.980
so I thought it might be a nice change of pace.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:20.700
It was my fault.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.400
I should have studied cooking more.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.100
Why did you pick that restaurant?

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:31.140
You knew that Mana girl lived there, didn't you?

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:35.840
I just wanted to see how those girls lived.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.410
Is that really it?

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.380
That's it.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.700
So, what about the job?

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.310
We can still cancel.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.300
Wow!

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.360
Makoto visited your home?

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.720
What a surprise.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.840
She definitely came to investigate us!

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.760
I don't think so...

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.310
Will Makopi be all right?

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.170
She messed up a little...

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:04.820
I'd call it more than a little.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.070
And she got sad after hearing what Grandpa said...

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:11.680
You must really like Makopi, huh?

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.280
I'm going to see Makopi!

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.580
Wait, Mana!

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.040
Stop!

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.250
You want to see her,

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.240
but do you even know where she is?

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.430
Well I guess... I don't.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:29.420
Oh, but that letter we got from her manager had a business card!

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:32.970
Then perhaps we should try the phone first.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.000
Yeah.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.710
Guess so.

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:38.320
I was about to do something dumb again.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.470
Huh?

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:40.970
Makopi!

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.760
I'm glad you came back!

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:47.390
What?

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:48.150
Hey,

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:52.400
do you want to practice making omelette rice together?

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:54.120
I know a lot of tricks!

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.640
Practice?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:00.120
I came back because I wanted to learn to cook right.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.330
Could you help me?

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.300
Sure!

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:05.790
Honestly, I'm so happy you came back!

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:09.960
Mana was waiting in worry for you, Makoto.

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:14.970
I just don't want to abandon a job before it's through.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:15.820
Fine,

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:18.140
but I'm still really happy!

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.080
Go ahead.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.580
Okay, I'll crack it.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.420
I think you're putting too much force into it.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:28.470
Force?

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.840
Watch me.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.420
You can break eggs without a lot of force.

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:38.780
Tap, tap, crack is the rhythm!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.430
Tap, tap, crack?

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.210
Yeah!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.720
You did it! {Everyone else}

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:51.720
I did it! {Makoto}

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.030
Excellent work!

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:54.720
One more time, Makopi!

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.570
Go ahead.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.230
You did it!

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:03.940
It's perfect! {Fuck yeah, you applaud that teenager for doing something most grade schoolers are capable of}

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:13.490
With carrots, you go tap, tap, tiptiptap.

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.470
Tip, tap, tiptiptap. {Why tiptiptap if she doesn't cut on the middle tip?}

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:17.940
With onions, you go tac, tac, tictictac.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.900
Tac tac, tictictac.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.970
Yeah, that was good!

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.500
You learn quickly!

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:27.140
She's gotta be Cure Sword!

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.580
So, they're connected?

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.390
Here.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.590
Use this.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:35.820
Thank you.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:38.660
Next, we're gonna cut the bacon!

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:40.600
I'll wash the rice.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.170
Then I shall prepare the seasoning.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:57.200
No matter what you do, you always fail when it counts.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.180
Sounds like you!

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.680
Who lost to them last time?

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:02.870
Oh yeah, you!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.440
Oh, I didn't lose.

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:13.330
I only <i>let</i> them win.

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.460
It's rotten.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.360
This is rotten?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.060
Not that.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.750
King Selfish'll be pissed.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.140
The time we've got left

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.170
isn't too much.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.600
Put some effort in!

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.770
How about <i>you</i>, huh?

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:34.220
What are you saying?

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.070
Good grief.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:38.950
Guess it's my turn.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.270
And we're filming!

00:10:56.270 --> 00:10:57.170
Action!

00:10:58.590 --> 00:10:59.680
Let's begin.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.980
<i>Tap, tap, tiptiptap.</i>

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.430
<i>Tap, tap, tiptiptap.</i>

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:13.790
<i>Tac, tac, tictictac.</i>

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:16.230
<i>Tac, tac, tictictac.</i>

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:17.530
<i>Tap, tap,</i>

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:18.560
<i>crack.</i>

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:19.760
<i>Tap, tap,</i>

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:20.610
<i>crack!</i>

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:25.480
Great, Makopi!

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.400
You've improved a lot overnight.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:30.060
Thank you very much.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.070
All right,

00:11:36.510 --> 00:11:39.290
let's get to the end in one take!

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:39.780
Right.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:44.040
All that's left is to wrap the chicken rice in the egg, correct?

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.230
But that's the hardest part!

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.040
Stay strong, Makopi!

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.360
<i>I'll show them.</i>

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:54.290
<i>Those girls practiced so much with me last night,</i>

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:56.070
<i>so I owe it to them. {starts on "ano kotachi"}</i>

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.050
Nice! {Rikka}

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.890
How impressive! {Alice}

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:20.490
You did it, Makopi!

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.650
It's huge!

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:24.770
Sorry!

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:27.350
I got the ingredients to feed four on accident!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.330
Aw, it doesn't matter.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:30.830
We're finally done,

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:33.690
so lets get some shots of you all eating it.

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:38.140
Well, Makopi, let's put on the finishing touch!

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.440
Here you go.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.030
What's this?

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.640
Use it like this.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.670
Like a smooch...

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.550
That's Mana for you.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:54.710
It's quite lovely!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:59.290
This makes it even tastier!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.920
Rikka, Alice, help me!

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:03.010
Sure!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:03.900
<i>Good.</i>

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.390
<i>Makoto's smile has returned.</i>

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.390
Dig in!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.420
Yummy!

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:14.280
It's quite tasty!

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:18.710
<i>It really is good!</i>

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.910
And it's her first time cooking, too. {Poor memory.}

00:13:22.210 --> 00:13:25.610
Those girls put their hearts into that omelette rice.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.710
'Course it's gonna be good.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.020
<i>My heart...</i>

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.590
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:38.380
<i>didn't I use to put my heart into my songs?</i>

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.490
<i>I wanted to see that person smile. {I can't tell if it's a dude or a chick, so meh.}</i>

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.670
<i>But lately...</i>

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.260
<i>I haven't been able to find that person,</i>

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.600
<i>and in my haste,</i>

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:52.900
<i>I forgot to put my heart into my singing.</i>

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:57.270
Makopi?

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.080
Is something wrong?

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.310
I remembered something important.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:03.950
Something important?

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.470
It's thanks to you three.

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.030
Makopi!

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.480
Oh, to be young.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:16.270
But that omelette rice looks tasty! {Imagine the show's star pedophile saying that line.}

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:21.510
Man, I could go for some fresh, homemade omelette rice.

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.980
I oughta ditch this job and get me some of that. {I can't wait to take this out of context.}

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:30.110
Nah, work's work.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.080
Just gotta deal.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.300
Aw, just eat it.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:37.730
Who's there?

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.260
I will grant...

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:42.270
your desire.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.760
Go berserk!

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.510
Release the darkness in your heart!

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:05.540
Oink!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.620
I wanna pig out!

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:08.610
What's that?

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:12.120
A dark heartbeat!

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.460
It's from the kitchen.

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:16.430
What the?!

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.260
Everyone, it is dangerous here.

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:20.820
Hurry outside.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.730
But the girls are still inside!

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.040
Worry not, they are safe.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:28.370
Now hurry.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:29.040
Right!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:33.850
Let's go, Charles!

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:34.950
